<div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">EUI's music engraver</span>
            <h1>Scores engraved <em>like LilyPond</em>, drawn in an instant.</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                <strong>eui-score</strong> reads the LilyPond language and engraves it into vector paths: staves,
                noteheads, beams, slurs, titles. The same source plays as MIDI and prints as an A4 PDF. A note it
                cannot engrave is refused, never silently dropped.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= examples_path() %>">See the <%= example_count %> examples</a>
                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="<%= playground_path() %>">Try the playground</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-sheet">
            <%- score_figure(hero, {"name": "syntax/home", "sandbox": playground_path(), "source": "closed"}) %>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="facts">
        <div class="fact"><strong>1.9 ms</strong><span>to engrave the exposition of Beethoven's Fifth, against 338 ms for the original Soli engraver</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>3 outputs</strong><span>the screen, a MIDI file and an A4 PDF, from a single source</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>0 fonts</strong><span>every glyph and every letter is an outline, placed where the engraving wants it</span></div>
        <div class="fact"><strong>2 %</strong><span>width difference with LilyPond 2.24, at the same staff size</span></div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">One source, three outputs</span>
            <h2>Write the music once.</h2>
            <p class="lead">The LilyPond text is the only thing an application keeps. Everything else is computed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3">
            <div class="card">
                <span class="card-num">i.</span>
                <h3>On screen</h3>
                <p><code>score(src, opts)</code> draws the score as EUI canvases, one per system: an edit redraws only the system it touches.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <span class="card-num">ii.</span>
                <h3>As MIDI</h3>
                <p><code>score_midi(src)</code> writes a Standard MIDI File, one track per staff, dynamics and hairpins included, as LilyPond's <code>\midi</code> would.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <span class="card-num">iii.</span>
                <h3>As PDF</h3>
                <p><code>score_pdf(src)</code> prints the A4 pages as vectors, with LilyPond's margins and page breaks, and no embedded font.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">In an EUI view</span>
            <h2>One line is enough.</h2>
            <p class="lead">The score is a catalogue widget like a button or a table. It follows the theme: its ink is a colour role.</p>
        </div>
<pre class="code-block"><code>score("\\relative c' { \\key g \\major \\time 3/4 g'4( a b) | d2. \\bar \"|.\" }",
      {"width": 640})</code></pre>
        <%- score_figure(hello, {"name": "syntax/hello", "sandbox": playground_path(), "source": "none"}) %>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">On any website</span>
            <h2>Two tags, and your page engraves.</h2>
            <p class="lead">
                Compiled to WebAssembly, the same engraver runs in the browser: no server, no account,
                207 KB gzipped, downloaded once.
            </p>
        </div>
<pre class="code-block"><code>&lt;script type="module" src="https://score.solisoft.net/eui-score/eui-score.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;eui-score&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/x-lilypond"&gt; \relative c' { c4 e g c | g1 \bar "|." } &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/eui-score&gt;</code></pre>
        <p><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="<%= embed_path() %>">Embed eui-score in your site →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
            <h2>From text to paths, in four steps.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline">
            <div class="step"><b>Read</b><span>The LilyPond subset is parsed; anything else is refused with its position.</span></div>
            <div class="step"><b>Space</b><span>LilyPond's columns: 1.2 staff spaces more each time a duration doubles.</span></div>
            <div class="step"><b>Place</b><span>Stems, beams quantised to the staff lines, slurs at LilyPond's height, aligned dynamics.</span></div>
            <div class="step"><b>Draw</b><span>Rectangles and Emmentaler outlines, in pixels: EUI canvas, SVG or PDF.</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">The gallery</span>
            <h2>From solos to the orchestra.</h2>
            <p class="lead">Every example is engraved on demand by the engraver, with its source, its MIDI and its PDF.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3">
            <% for cat in categories %>
                <a class="card" href="<%= example_category_path(cat["slug"]) %>">
                    <h3><%= cat["title"] %></h3>
                    <p><%= cat["lead"] %></p>
                    <span class="card-count"><%= cat["count"] %> scores →</span>
                </a>
            <% end %>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
